Bavaria: Woman missing for 30 years - police dig for body parts
More than 30 years after the disappearance of a then 18-year-old from Naila (Hof district), police are looking for the woman's remains.
Emergency forces dug up a road at Marxgrün on Saturday.
For this purpose, the pavement and several layers below were removed, as the police and prosecutors jointly announced.
According to new findings, the missing person may not have been buried far away from her place of residence at the time.
The woman has disappeared since November 4, 1986.
Investigators didn't rule out a crime at the time either.
Since last year, the criminal police Hof together with the public prosecutor’s office is working intensively on the case.
Together with scientists from the Technical University of Munich and the Bavarian Monument Protection Authority, the investigators encountered a conspicuousness under the street at Marxgrün by means of a ground radar.
With the help of a dog trained on the smell of human bones, the officers narrowed the spot to a few meters.
The results of the excavations should be announced later in the afternoon.
