Billerbeck: 500 lids for a life without paralysis
Since the beginning of the new school year, the Ludgeri School has been involved in the "Lid against polio - 500 covers for a life without polio".
Polio is the abbreviation for poliomyelitis, an infectious disease caused by polioviruses.
The disease referred to in German as polio leads from signs of paralysis to death.
In Germany, polio is considered eradicated, but there are still three countries worldwide where the disease occurs.
The cause of poliomyelitis, the polioviruses, so far can only be contained by vaccinations, according to a press release.
