After all, the graduation service for the bikers was on the agenda.
Frank Schröder is the motor pastor within the Evangelical Church of Westphalia and thus responsible for the pastoral interests of PS-strong two-cyclists.
Between April and September the traditional motorcycle service (MoGo) takes place on the last Sunday of a month at Haus Nordhelle.
Bikers traditionally celebrate the end of the season in the Church of Peace in Eveking.
Around 150 bikers had gathered there on Sunday to commit anything but ordinary service.
As early as 10 a.m., the cars were lined up in front of the church's entrance portal.
Initially, the biker breakfast was on the program and it could be strengthened with coffee and cake or already with a hefty curry sausage.
