The extensive exclusion of the German public had "strengthened many reservations."
Heimatverein Nottuln: Offer has already established itself
After the long summer break, it's finally folk meeting time again.
On 18 October (Thursday) at 19.30, the Heimatverein Nottuln organizes its fifth Nottulner folk meeting in the fireplace room of the Alte Amtmannei.
It’s been a year since wen’t worked for the first time.
In the meantime, this event has become an integral part of the musical event calendar in Nottuln," says Hanns Moormann, chairman of the Nottulner Heimatverein.
I would not have thought that our folk meeting would establish itself so quickly in Nottuln.
Whether Sturmtief Friederike in January or heatwave in July, the fireplace room of the Amtmannei was always fully occupied.
"As always, the program at the next Folktreff is a colourful mixture of German folk, hiking and sailor's songs, folk songs, evergreens and old hits," says Karl-Heinz Stevermüer, who invites musicians who are always friends to Nottuln.
Klaus Spellmeyer has agreed with his accordion for the first folk meeting "birthday".
For many years he was a member of "Gaitling", a group from the neighbouring district of Steinfurt, who played music with Low German texts.
Now he's traveling with an Irish-folk band.
The creators of the Folktreff are happy to remember the last event in the summer, when Christoph Schulz from Folktreff Emsdetten thrilled listeners with his international version of the song "Frösche in der Nacht" and sent them home with an earworm.
"We expect many cheerful guests to once again spend a convivial and humorous evening," reads the invitation of the Heimatverein.
Anyone who plays an instrument and wants to get actively involved is invited to participate.
Since the sought-after seats are always occupied quickly, it is advisable to be there early enough.
The Folktreff starts at 19.30 o'clock, but admission is already at 19 o'clock.
