Macedonians vote on new state name
In Macedonia today, around 1.8 million citizens are voting on whether to change their country's name in North Macedonia.
In the event of a yes, the nearly three-decade-smoldering conflict with its neighbour Greece could be resolved.
Athens had insisted on a name change because of its northern province of the same name, blocking any rapprochement of Macedonia to the West.
Voters, therefore, will also decide on future western integration.
The U.S. had announced that the country could quickly become a NATO member in the event of a positive outcome of the referendum.
Syrians in Custody.
Refugee attacked three women.
A Syrian brutally beaten up to three pensioners and severely injured them as a result.
The 41-year-old asylum seeker had rioted on Friday at around 2 p.m. in the escape lane in Alsergrund.
When the officers arrived, they spoke to the accused, who went with clenched fists on passers-by and tried to attack them, to his behavior.
As a result, the Syrian attempted to punch and kick the officers.
A little later, it turned out that the suspect had knocked three elderly ladies (65, 67, 75) with his fists to the ground shortly before in Währinger Straße at a tram stop.
In addition, he had kicked the trio with his feet.
