He was taken to the hospital and monitored continuously during treatment.
SPD Politician: Johannes Kahrs marries his friend
Almost exactly one year after the entry into force of the marriage for everyone, the SPD politician Johannes Kahrs has married his long-term friend Christoph Rohde.
The two said yes on Saturday in Hamburg.
A registered civil partnership was out of the question for them, Kahrs had previously told the "Bild" newspaper.
"If we get married, that's right." He's been with his partner for 25 years.
The 55-year-old Kahrs is fiscal policy spokesman of the SPD parliamentary group and one of the spokespersons of the Seeheimer Kreis, the conservative SPD wing.
In the Bundestag debate on the opening of marriage to homosexuals, Kahrs had caused a stir on June 30, 2017 with a rage speech.
For example, he had accused German Chancellor Angela Merkel (CDU) of "stumbling up" on the issue.
"That's your Schabowski moment," he said, alluding to Günter Schabowski's accidental proclamation of the GDR border opening.
Since October 1, 2017, same-sex couples have been able to get married just like heterosexuals.
Previously, they had been able to register their civil partnership since 2001, but there was no equality with marriage, for example on adoption law.
