In total, 50 plots for single and semi-detached houses will be created on the site in the south of Landsham, as well as four areas for multi-family houses with eight residential unitions each.
The development is now almost completed, the roads and paths will soon be paved.
A single plot and two of the apartment buildings belong to one private person, the rest of the municipality of Pliening.
It sells the majority on the open market, 20 plots in the social-friendly model.
According to Frick, the two apartment buildings of the municipality are to be erected as affordable housing.
With a total of 16 income-oriented apartments sponsored by the Free State.
Space for 200 people
Roughly estimated on the area of the Landsham-Süd development area, housing for about 200 people is created.
Not only that: now, at the beginning of October, according to Frick, the start for the new construction of a daycare center.
It will house three kindergarten and three crèche groups as well as a multi-purpose room.
The opening is scheduled for September 2019, at the start of the next kindergarten year.
This is how Schalke's Naldo "great sport" also succeeds on the bench
For the third time in a row not in the starting eleven: Naldo thanks Schalke coach Domenico Tedesco.
Gelsenkirchen - After Ronaldo Aparecido Rodrigues had sat for the third time in a row not in the Schalker starting eleven, but on the bench, it would have been great for many people if the almost two-meter-tall Brazilian had really spoken the frustration of the soul.
But when the Schalk players gathered in the middle circle as usual after the 1:0 win over FSV Mainz 05 and head coach Domenico Tedesco thanked all his pros, the 36-year-old, whom everyone simply calls Naldo, intervened and said; "We have to thank, coach!"
"That was very emotional, that was great sport," Tedesco later said of the reaction to his vice-captain, who had no resentment despite his reservious existence.
Naldo, who was hailed last season as the best Schalker, knows that he actually didn't get on the siding with his coach - but gets a break for good reasons.
One reason called "burden control."
It wasn't easy to tell him that
"It wasn't easy to tell him this, I'll tell you honestly," Tedesco reported from the moment he told Naldo that he wasn't in the starting eleven.
He's an important player, he's an important person.
But it's always about the matter, it's about the club," Tedesco justified the move.
Naldo has played 90 minutes against Bayern and Porto.
He's 36 years old.
It is important that at the moment everyone can take a breather.
And that we all keep in the boat," Tedesco explained the rotation, which has also caught Naldo most recently.
And to which the Brazilian reacted with the wisdom of his advanced age: by also proving himself on the benck as an exemplary team player.
The mood in Austria's industry continued its decline in August compared to the eurozone.
The Purchasing Manager's Index (PMI) was at 46.7 points at a 37-month low.
Europe-wide, however, Austria still has the third-best mood behind Ireland and the Netherlands, the Markit Institute said on its survey of 3,000 companies on Monday.
Unlike in Austria, the PMI of the euro zone rose by 1.1 points to 45.1 points, the index is still below the mark of 50 points for the 13th month in a row, which indicates growth.
Only Ireland's industry cracked that threshold with 50.9 points in August.
The Greeks (42.1 points) were the final lights.
In Germany, France and Spain, the mood barometer declined, but more slowly than in the months before.
In Spain, the index reached its highest level at 44.0 points since March.
"The slightly weakened descent could mean that the worst has survived," Markit economist Rob Dobson said.
However, the industry remains - in the third quarter anyway - growth brake number one.
A rapid return to the growth zone is not in sight: export orders in the eurozone have fallen more sharply than it has been since November 2011.
For this reason, the companies cut jobs for the seventh month in a row.
Industrial production in China also declined more sharply in August than initially thought.
The sentiment barometer fell to 47.6 points from 49.3 points the previous month.
Experts had initially expected 47.8 points.
The Purchasing Managers' Index bases its figures on representative surveys of 3,000 European industrial companies.
Among other things, developments in sales, employment, warehouses and prices will be raised.
Tuchel's PSG team manages eighth victory in eighth league game
29 September 2018 at 19:45
Nice coach Thomas Tuchel rushes further from victory to victory with Paris Saint-Germain in France's football championship.
At the OGC Nice, the defending champion won with 3:0 (1:0) thanks to two hits from superstar Neymar and was thus also successful in the eighth league game.
Olympique Lyon had made such a good start to the season in France 82 years ago.
Brazilian Neymar put PSG in the lead after 22 minutes and made the final score in the aftermath.
Christopher Nkunku (46.) ensured the interim 2:0.
In doing so, Paris also managed the dress rehearsal for Wednesday's groundbreaking second Champions League group game against Red Star Belgrade.
At the start of the premier class, Tuchel's team had to accept the only mandatory game defeat so far at 2:3 in Liverpool so far this season.
